# Copy this file to .env and fill it in. .env is never uploaded (see .gitignore).
# Your own Claude API key (console.anthropic.com): Claude Haiku 5.5 checks each offer's reason, writes eBay listings
# and judges how bad a UK price's damage is; Claude Sonnet 5.5 fixes a flagged reason, decides how bad the damage is
# when code and Haiku disagree, and steps in when this computer's models can't. You pay Anthropic for what you use.
# Without it, everything runs on this computer (FlipAssist's own models, Gemma 3 4B and code). Put it after the = sign:
# anything there counts as a key, so leave it empty if you have none.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# The dollar-to-pound rate the cost meter uses. Change it when the rate moves.
USD_TO_GBP=0.80
# The key every caller of the API (flip.api) must send in an X-API-Key header: 32 characters or more,
# or the API refuses every call. The app makes one by itself on first launch (launcher/), so you only need this
# to call the API some other way. Make a random one and paste it after the = sign:
#   .venv/bin/python -c "import secrets; print(secrets.token_urlsafe(32))"
FLIP_API_KEY=
# UK prices for iPhones, Samsung phones and MacBooks work with no key: they're free, from the AlertFlip prices API,
# refreshed about monthly. FLIP_PUBLIC_PRICES=off turns them off.
FLIP_PUBLIC_PRICES=
# Your own AlertFlip prices API, if you have one: its address and its key. With PRICES_KEY set, it's asked in place of
# the free prices, as before. Leave both empty for the free ones.
PRICES_URL=
PRICES_KEY=
# Only to ask eBay UK again for each category's fields (python -m flip.ebay --refresh): your eBay
# developer app's production keys. Drafting never needs them: it uses data/ebay_fields.json.
EBAY_CLIENT_ID=
EBAY_CLIENT_SECRET=
